---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "Printable Amps to Watts Conversion Chart | Ampstowatt";
const description = "Get a quick reference cheat sheet for converting amps to watts at 12V, 120V, and 240V. Perfect for toolboxes and electrical planning.";
const h1Title = "Printable Amps to Watts Conversion Chart";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/blog/amps-to-watts-conversion-chart-pdf/"
  h1Title={h1Title}
  kicker="Reference Guide"
>
  <article class="article-content">
    <h1>{h1Title}</h1>
    
    <div class="article-header-meta">
      <span>By AmpsToWatt Engineering</span>
      <span>•</span>
      <span>Updated: June 2026</span>
    </div>

    <p>Whether you're an electrician in the field, a DIY home renovator, or designing an off-grid solar system, having quick access to amperage-to-wattage conversions saves time and prevents dangerous overloads.</p>
    
    <p>Below is a comprehensive, print-friendly cheat sheet covering the most common voltages: 12V (DC/Solar), 120V (Standard US), and 240V (High-Power US). You can print this page directly using your browser's print function (Ctrl+P / Cmd+P) to keep a copy in your toolbox or stick it inside your breaker panel door.</p>

    <div class="print-friendly-area" style="border: 2px dashed var(--cyan); padding: 2.5rem; margin: 3rem 0; background: var(--surface-2); border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);">
      <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 0; color: var(--gold); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 1rem;">Amps to Watts Cheat Sheet</h2>
      
      <h3 style="margin-top: 2rem;">12V DC (Automotive, Solar, RV)</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--muted); margin-top: -0.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; font-family: var(--mono);">Formula: Watts = Amps × 12</p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Current (Amps)</th>
            <th>Power (Watts)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>1 Amp</td><td>12 W</td></tr>
          <tr><td>5 Amps</td><td>60 W</td></tr>
          <tr><td>10 Amps</td><td>120 W</td></tr>
          <tr><td>20 Amps</td><td>240 W</td></tr>
          <tr><td>50 Amps</td><td>600 W</td></tr>
          <tr><td>100 Amps</td><td>1,200 W</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h3 style="margin-top: 3rem;">120V AC (Standard US Household)</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--muted); margin-top: -0.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; font-family: var(--mono);">Formula: Watts = Amps × 120 (Assuming PF=1.0)</p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Current (Amps)</th>
            <th>Power (Watts)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>1 Amp</td><td>120 W</td></tr>
          <tr><td>5 Amps</td><td>600 W</td></tr>
          <tr><td>10 Amps</td><td>1,200 W</td></tr>
          <tr><td>15 Amps (Standard Breaker)</td><td>1,800 W</td></tr>
          <tr><td>20 Amps (Kitchen Breaker)</td><td>2,400 W</td></tr>
          <tr><td>30 Amps (RV Hookup)</td><td>3,600 W</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h3 style="margin-top: 3rem;">240V AC (High-Power Appliances & EVs)</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--muted); margin-top: -0.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; font-family: var(--mono);">Formula: Watts = Amps × 240 (Assuming PF=1.0)</p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Current (Amps)</th>
            <th>Power (Watts)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>10 Amps</td><td>2,400 W</td></tr>
          <tr><td>20 Amps</td><td>4,800 W</td></tr>
          <tr><td>30 Amps (Dryer/Water Heater)</td><td>7,200 W</td></tr>
          <tr><td>40 Amps (Oven/Range)</td><td>9,600 W</td></tr>
          <tr><td>50 Amps (EV Charger)</td><td>12,000 W</td></tr>
          <tr><td>100 Amps (Subpanel)</td><td>24,000 W</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <style>
      @media print {
        body * {
          visibility: hidden;
        }
        .print-friendly-area, .print-friendly-area * {
          visibility: visible;
          color: black !important;
          background: white !important;
        }
        .print-friendly-area {
          position: absolute;
          left: 0;
          top: 0;
          width: 100%;
          border: none !important;
          box-shadow: none !important;
        }
        .print-friendly-area th {
          background: #f0f0f0 !important;
          border-bottom: 2px solid black !important;
        }
        .print-friendly-area td {
          border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc !important;
        }
      }
    </style>

    <div class="pro-tip">
      <strong>Need a different voltage?</strong>
      <p>Check out our comprehensive interactive <a href="/conversion-charts/">Conversion Charts</a> page or use the <a href="/">Calculator Suite</a> to find the exact wattage for any voltage and power factor.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
